  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Capacities of the Ports of Aden and Mukalla UNDP-YEM-01003133 (ECaPAM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ECaPAM project is a critical UNDP-led initiative aiming to revitalize two essential ports in war-torn Yemen, improving the flow of essential goods and humanitarian aid. By rehabilitating damaged infrastructure, including a marine workshop in Aden, procuring vital equipment like mooring boats and tugboats, and enhancing operational efficiency through activities such as staff training in hydrographic surveying, the project aims to reduce waiting times and facilitate a smooth flow of supplies</narrative>
  </description>
